    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Trained from childhood by his great-aunt Tia Oberta (a withered @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.revenants.JournalEntry.ldyqw2o2gR45LxDO]{Obertus} revenant witch) at horrific personal cost to himself and his family, Esteban rejected Vicissitude-as-purity, briefly joined the Children of the Dracon, then found the Old World's koldun hidebound and useless. The 1985 Mexico City earthquake was his breakthrough: he felt the earth's death throes and unlocked new koldunic power. After the @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.jaYCq9rVOh0I9NCN]{Tremere} antitribu chantry of Elena Vasquez vanished, Esteban and the Harbinger of Skulls La Viuda Blanca broke in and recovered much of her thaumaturgical library, making him one of the best-informed occultists in Mexico.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Esteban believes cataclysms have always served him and looks forward to the coming ones. He plays a precarious political balancing act between Old World koldun patrons, cardinals, and seraphs who all expect future service, while keeping Tia Oberta \u2014 limbless but alive on infusions of his blood \u2014 in a hidden closet-shrine beneath the northern colonias.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Rafaela Lapaz. Pack-bonded (Vaulderie) with La Viuda Blanca. Disciplines as printed: Auspex 3, Koldunic Sorcery 4, Thaumaturgy 1, Vicissitude 1; Koldunic Paths: Way of Earth 4 (primary), Way of Water 3; Thaumaturgical Paths: Path of the Father's Vengeance 1 (primary).",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
